# Chroma library, modern Earth: the faith sphere's events as they touch a life (Library thread, 2026-10-09, "v22" update
# stage 4, item 15 phase 3). Design: chroma-ideas/spheres-implementation.md sections 2, 4 "Library" and 5; data:
# chroma-ideas/spheres-data/faith.json (events: wording.modern and on_character). Fields: build.py (WORLD_SIT,
# WORLD_OPT, the spheres' sphere:, haunt:, ladder:, sphere_event:).
#
# Every moment here is an event moment: a life event the Engine fires on its faith event (sphere_event:) for the people
# the '# world:' line's selector names; per_year is all 0 (they exist only with the world on) and there are no drivers.
# The '# world:' line names the event key, the selector and the share of selected people who get the moment (estimate).
# Every moment carries sphere: faith; every option carries the face it acts in (faith.X for a one-colour option, the
# pair face in wheel order for a pair option, so WG takes faith.GW, WR faith.RW and UG faith.GU).
#
# One moment for each of the 22 faith events with a modern epoch and an on_character line, except three the world
# already fires: faith_revival ("a revival fills the square", earth-world-eras.lib), new_teaching ("a new faith comes
# to town", C5 in earth-world-institutions.lib) and schism ("the congregation splits in two", earth-world-wants.lib,
# the same split over who leads, one half keeping the building). coming_of_age is told from the family's side, since
# the young person's own rite is the everyday "a coming-of-age ceremony".
#
# Layout: five one-colour options and one pair set in every moment; the twelve D1-D6 halves are each used once or
# twice. Evenness: in every moment the five one-colour options share one chance and the five pair options another
# (each colour sits in exactly two pairs), so every colour has the same mean chance in each moment and in every stage.
# No flags.
#
# No real faith is named and no one culture's festival; faith conflict is told indirectly (a broken shop window, a
# banned neighbour's books, a quarrel over a wedding). The scandal is about money. Claims of wonders are told as what
# people say.
#
# share: on every moment (2026-10-10, Engine phase 3a) is its '# world:' share: the engine draws at birth who can
# ever meet it, so when the event comes to town only that share of the people there are open to the moment.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- coming_of_age (pairs D3a)

# world: sphere event coming_of_age, selector members, share .5
== the young one's rite of passage
tier: life event
sphere: faith
sphere_event: coming_of_age
share: .5
at: faith body
stages: adult mature
age: 35-65
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
times: World event: coming_of_age (sphere faith). Fires for members of a faith that keeps its rites when a young person of their household reaches the age the faith marks; a parent in such a faith sees one to three children through it (estimate); share .5
likelier: a family that keeps the faith; a close congregation; several children in the house
rarer: a family that keeps the faith in name only; a scattered family; few children
gap: 2-10
tone: joy
life: faith, family, rites
horizon: months
roles: child, parent
earth: your child reaches the age your faith marks, and the rite, the class and the party all fall to the family
scene: {child} has reached the age the faith marks. The ceremony is short; the party will last all afternoon. {parent} has already cried once and will not say why.
scene W: {N} has helped {child} learn every word of the rite, and wants the day to go exactly as it should.
scene U: {child} keeps asking what the words of the rite actually mean, and {N} is not sure they can say.
scene B: The whole congregation will be watching, and families are judged by how such a day is kept. {N} has a budget in mind and a guest list.
scene R: {child} is nervous and excited at once, and {N} remembers how their own rite felt: like a door swinging open.
scene G: The same words were said over {N}, and over {parent} before them. Today they will be said over {child}.
- W | go over the rite's words with the young one each evening until they are sure | v: tradition, conformity | lever: loyalty | pushes: belief | sphere: faith.W | chance: 70
- U | explain to the young one what each part of the rite means, and why | v: universalism, self-direction | sphere: faith.U | chance: 70
- B | throw the biggest party the street has seen, and invite the people who matter | v: achievement, power | sphere: faith.B | chance: 70
- R | stand up at the party and give a speech that has the whole room in tears | v: stimulation, benevolence | sphere: faith.R | chance: 70
- G | bring out the old family keepsake, and pass it on at the end of the rite | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: faith.G | chance: 70
- BG | spend beyond the family's means, so the family is not outdone | v: power, tradition | sphere: faith.BG | chance: 60
- RG | take the young one and friends out for a night under the sky, as of old | v: tradition, stimulation | sphere: faith.RG | chance: 60
- UB | ask a respected elder to take the young one under their wing from now on | v: achievement, security | sphere: faith.UB | chance: 60
- WR | gather every relative under one roof for the day, even the ones who stopped speaking | v: benevolence, tradition | pushes: close | sphere: faith.RW | chance: 60
- WU | sit in on the class before the rite, and help the teacher with the nervous ones | v: conformity, universalism | sphere: faith.WU | chance: 60
works: The day goes well, and {child} carries something from it that will last.
works: Years later {child} still talks about the rite, and about who stood beside them that day.
fails: A family quarrel spoils the afternoon, and that is what {child} remembers most.
fails: The rite passes in a blur of costs and nerves, and nobody quite enjoys it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- pilgrimage (pairs D5b)

# world: sphere event pilgrimage, selector place, share .15
== the old walking road is full again
tier: life event
sphere: faith
sphere_event: pilgrimage
share: .15
haunt: faith.shrines
holy: pilgrimage
at: faith body
stages: juvenile+
age: 16-80
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
times: World event: pilgrimage (sphere faith). Fires for the people of a place on or near a pilgrim road in the walking season of a safe, well-off year; most people never walk one, and of those near a busy road perhaps 1 in 7 sets out in a given season (estimate); share .15
likelier: a town on an old pilgrim road; a promise made in a hard year; a question carried for years; good health
rarer: poor health; small children at home; a lean year; a person far from any road
gap: 5-30
tone: joy
life: faith, travel, friendship
horizon: week
roles: friend, parent
earth: the old pilgrim road is busy this season, and a friend offers you a place in a group walking to the shrine
scene: The old walking road is full again this season: believers, seekers and the merely curious, all with blisters. {friend} has a spare place in a group setting off next week, three weeks on foot to the shrine.
scene W: {N} made a promise last year, when things were bad, to walk the road if they came right. They did.
scene U: {N} has a question that has followed them for years. Perhaps three weeks of walking will settle it.
scene B: The road is a long walk, and also a long run of inns, guides and strangers worth knowing. {N} sees both.
scene R: {N} wants to go simply for the going: the road, the dust, the singing round the fire at night.
scene G: {parent} walked the road when young, and still keeps a shell from the shrine on the windowsill.
- W | walk the whole road to keep the promise you made, every step of it | v: tradition, conformity | mark: kept your word | lever: loyalty | sphere: faith.W | chance: 65
- U | walk with a notebook, and ask each pilgrim why they came | v: self-direction, universalism | sphere: faith.U | chance: 65
- B | go as a paid guide for a group of first-timers | v: achievement | sphere: faith.B | chance: 65
- R | set off alone at dawn, with no plan for where to sleep | v: stimulation, self-direction | mark: took a wild risk | sphere: faith.R | chance: 65
- G | carry a stone from the family graves and leave it at the shrine | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: faith.G | chance: 65
- BR | sell cold drinks and blister plasters at the steepest bend of the road | v: achievement, hedonism | sphere: faith.BR | chance: 55
- RG | walk the last stretch barefoot, the way the old pilgrims did | v: tradition, stimulation | sphere: faith.RG | chance: 55
- UG | fall in beside an old pilgrim and learn the road's stories as you walk | v: tradition, universalism | sphere: faith.GU | chance: 55
- WB | help run the pilgrims' hostel for the season, and keep its books straight | v: security, benevolence | sphere: faith.WB | chance: 55
- WU | learn the road's old prayers by heart before setting out | v: tradition, conformity | mark: learned a skill | sphere: faith.WU | chance: 55
works: {N} comes home footsore and lighter, with friends from three towns away.
works: Somewhere on the road the question {N} carried quietly settles.
fails: Blisters, rain and a quarrel in the group, and {N} turns back halfway.
fails: The road is so crowded that {N} finds no quiet on it at all.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- scandal (pairs D4a)

# world: sphere event scandal, selector members, share .6
== the building fund is gone
tier: life event
sphere: faith
sphere_event: scandal
share: .6
haunt: faith.congregation
at: faith body
stages: juvenile+
age: 14-100
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
times: World event: scandal (sphere faith). Fires for the members of a congregation whose house is rich and badly overseen when an insider or the press brings a misuse of its money to light; a lifelong member lives through one perhaps once in a life (estimate); share .6
likelier: a rich house with loose oversight; a leader in post for decades; a free press in town
rarer: a small house that counts its money in the open; a closed regime that silences the press
gap: 15-40
tone: trouble
life: faith, community, money
horizon: months
roles: grandparent, friend
earth: the news breaks that your congregation's leader spent the building fund on himself, and half the seats go empty
scene: The news breaks on a weekday: the congregation's leader spent the building fund on a house and a car for himself. By the next rest day half the seats are empty, and everyone asks who else knew.
scene W: {N} has given to that fund every month for years, and kept the rules the leader preached.
scene U: {N} wants to see the accounts, all of them, before believing anything either way.
scene B: The leader is finished. Someone will have to take over the board, and the board decides a great deal.
scene R: {N} feels the anger rise: all those sermons on honesty, and this.
scene G: {grandparent} helped build the old hall with their own hands. "The house is not the man," {grandparent} says.
- W | stand up at the members' meeting and ask the leader to step down | v: conformity, universalism | lever: voice | pushes: group congregation | sphere: faith.W | chance: 60
- U | ask to see the accounts, and go through them line by line | v: self-direction, universalism | lever: voice | pushes: institution faith body | sphere: faith.U | chance: 60
- B | put your name forward for the board while the old one falls | v: power, achievement | lever: lead | sphere: faith.B | chance: 60
- R | tell the leader to their face, in front of everyone, what you think of them | v: stimulation, universalism | mark: made an enemy | lever: voice | sphere: faith.R | chance: 60
- G | keep coming on the holy days, for the sake of the old hall | v: tradition, security | lever: loyalty | pushes: group congregation | sphere: faith.G | chance: 60
- BG | quietly move the family to another house of worship across town | v: security | lever: exit | sphere: faith.BG | chance: 50
- RG | stop going, and spend the rest day with the family instead | v: hedonism, tradition | lever: neglect | sphere: faith.RG | chance: 50
- UR | tell a reporter what you know about where the fund went | v: universalism, self-direction | mark: defied an authority | lever: voice | pushes: culture | sphere: faith.UR | chance: 50
- WB | push for an outside auditor and new rules on every fund | v: security, conformity | lever: voice | pushes: institution faith body | sphere: faith.WB | chance: 50
- WU | help draw up a fair plan to pay the givers back | v: universalism, benevolence | sphere: faith.WU | chance: 50
works: The worst comes out and is dealt with, and {N} can still look the congregation in the eye.
works: A year on the seats are filling again, under rules that keep the money in sight.
fails: The quarrel over who knew splits old friends, and {N} is caught in the middle of it.
fails: Nothing changes but the faces at the front, and {N} stops believing it ever will.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- faith_outlawed (pairs D6a)

# world: sphere event faith_outlawed, selector place, share .3
== a box of books from next door
tier: life event
sphere: faith
sphere_event: faith_outlawed
share: .3
at: faith body
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-100
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
times: World event: faith_outlawed (sphere faith). Fires for the people of a place when the rule lists a faith as dangerous; rare in settled times, and most who live through it meet it through a neighbour or a colleague (estimate); share .3
likelier: a regime short on tolerance; a faith tied to an enemy abroad or a revolt; an established faith pressing for a ban
rarer: a free and settled country; high trust; a town with no members of the listed faith
gap: 20-60
tone: trouble
life: faith, neighbours, law
horizon: months
roles: parent
earth: the government lists your neighbours' faith as dangerous, and they ask you to hide a box of their books
scene: The government has listed the faith of the family next door as dangerous. The father has lost his job, and they pray behind drawn curtains now. Tonight the mother knocks with a box of books and asks {N} to keep it for a while.
scene W: The law is the law, {N} was taught. But the family next door has never done anyone harm.
scene U: {N} reads the order twice. Nothing in it says what the faith has actually done.
scene B: A box like that could cost {N} a great deal, or buy goodwill in the right office.
scene R: {N} feels a hot rush of anger at the order, and at the fear in the neighbour's face.
scene G: {parent} remembers other lists in other years. "Families look after families," {parent} says.
- W | keep the box, and tell the family they are still welcome at your table | v: benevolence, universalism | mark: helped someone in need | lever: subvert | pushes: close | sphere: faith.W | chance: 55
- U | find a lawyer who will take the family's case against the order | v: universalism, self-direction | mark: helped someone in need | lever: voice | pushes: state | sphere: faith.U | chance: 55
- B | hand the box to the authorities, and keep your own record clean | v: security, power | mark: refused someone in need | sphere: faith.B | chance: 55
- R | join the crowd outside the town hall calling for the order to go | v: universalism, stimulation | lever: voice | pushes: state | sphere: faith.R | chance: 55
- G | say no to the box, but bring the family bread every week | v: benevolence, security | mark: helped someone in need | sphere: faith.G | chance: 55
- BG | hide the books under the floorboards, and say nothing to anyone | v: security, benevolence | lever: subvert | sphere: faith.BG | chance: 45
- UG | let the family hold their prayers in your back room on rest days | v: universalism, benevolence | mark: defied an authority | lever: subvert | sphere: faith.GU | chance: 45
- UR | write up the family's story without names, and send it to the papers | v: universalism, self-direction | lever: voice | pushes: culture | sphere: faith.UR | chance: 45
- WB | ask a friend in the council office how the family can appeal | v: security, benevolence | lever: voice | pushes: institution council | sphere: faith.WB | chance: 45
- WR | stand on the step beside the family when the officers come to call | v: benevolence, universalism | mark: defied an authority | sphere: faith.RW | chance: 45
works: The family gets through the hard years, and does not forget who stood by them.
works: In time the order is lifted, and {N} knows what part they played.
fails: Word gets round the street, and {N} is watched with suspicion for a long time.
fails: The family leaves town in the night, and {N} never learns where they went.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- tolerance (pairs D1b)

# world: sphere event tolerance, selector place, share .4
== the leaders of every faith share a meal
tier: life event
sphere: faith
sphere_event: tolerance
share: .4
at: faith body
stages: juvenile+
age: 14-100
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
times: World event: tolerance (sphere faith). Fires for the people of a place when, after a costly quarrel between faiths or when trade needs everyone, the rule and the faiths' leaders make peace; a person lives through such a turn once in a life at most (estimate); share .4
likelier: a town of several faiths; a quarrel lately ended; good trade; leaders who know each other
rarer: a town of one faith; a fresh grievance; hard times
gap: 20-60
tone: joy
life: faith, community, friendship
horizon: months
roles: friend, grandparent
earth: the leaders of every faith in your town share a meal, and your friend of another faith can now marry openly
scene: The leaders of every faith in town share a meal, and it makes the local paper. It is a start. {friend}, whose family keeps another faith, can now plan a wedding openly, and feasts from every side fill the town's year.
scene W: {N} was raised to keep to their own. The new peace asks for a wider courtesy, and {N} means to keep it properly.
scene U: {N} has always wondered what the neighbours believe. Now people are asking each other.
scene B: Open doors between the faiths mean new customers, new partners and friends in useful places.
scene R: The streets are louder and brighter with every faith's feast. {N} wants to be at all of them.
scene G: {grandparent} remembers when the faiths of the town shared one market and one well, before the bad years.
- W | invite a family of another faith to share your holy day meal | v: benevolence, tradition | sphere: faith.W | chance: 70
- U | join a circle that reads each faith's teachings together, one evening a month | v: universalism, self-direction | sphere: faith.U | chance: 70
- B | open your shop on every faith's feast days, with something for each | v: achievement | sphere: faith.B | chance: 70
- R | go to every feast in town this year, whoever is hosting | v: stimulation, hedonism | sphere: faith.R | chance: 70
- G | keep your own feasts as always, and greet the others warmly in the street | v: tradition, security | lever: loyalty | sphere: faith.G | chance: 70
- RG | dance at your friend's wedding, whatever the old aunts say | v: benevolence, hedonism | mark: made a friend | sphere: faith.RG | chance: 60
- UB | broker a deal for the faiths to share the empty hall on different days | v: achievement, universalism | sphere: faith.UB | chance: 60
- UR | write to the paper about the shared meal, and ask for another next year | v: universalism, self-direction | lever: voice | pushes: culture | sphere: faith.UR | chance: 60
- WB | ask the council to put every faith's holy days in the town calendar | v: universalism, conformity | lever: voice | pushes: institution council | sphere: faith.WB | chance: 60
- WG | help cook for a feast that the two faiths of the street share | v: benevolence, tradition | sphere: faith.GW | chance: 60
works: The peace holds, and {N} has friends now across a line that once seemed fixed.
works: A year on, the shared meal has become a habit of the town, and {N} is part of it.
fails: Old suspicions return with the first bad news, and the shared tables empty again.
fails: The others welcome {N}, but at home {N} is scolded for it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- sign (pairs D2b)

# world: sphere event sign, selector place, share .4
== a face in the window
tier: life event
sphere: faith
sphere_event: sign
share: .4
at: faith body
stages: juvenile+
age: 14-100
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
times: World event: sign (sphere faith). Fires for the people of a place when a claimed sign (a healing, a light, a vision) is taken up, most where devotion is high and fear is wide; a town sees one that draws crowds perhaps once in a generation (estimate); share .4
likelier: devout towns; fearful times; an illness in the family; a clip that spreads online
rarer: a town where few believe; settled times; a sceptical press
gap: 15-50
tone: mixed
life: faith, family, community
horizon: months
roles: grandparent
earth: people say a holy face has appeared in an old window, cars line the road, and your grandparent says their pain has eased
scene: A clip of what people say is a holy face in an old window has gone everywhere. By the weekend cars line the road outside, and {grandparent} says the pain in their hip eased after praying there. Nobody can say what happened.
scene W: The faith's elders have asked people to be careful what they claim, and to come to the regular rites instead.
scene U: {N} watches the clip frame by frame. Light, old glass, and a crowd that wants to see something. Or something else.
scene B: Thousands of visitors need parking, food, candles and somewhere to stay. Someone will do well out of it.
scene R: {N} stands in the crowd at dusk and feels the hair rise on their arms as the singing starts.
scene G: {grandparent} lights a candle for the dead at the window every evening now, and asks {N} to come too.
- W | ask the elders to keep the crowds orderly and the claims modest | v: security, conformity | lever: voice | pushes: belief | sphere: faith.W | chance: 65
- U | look into what the window really shows before believing or scoffing | v: self-direction, universalism | sphere: faith.U | chance: 65
- B | rent out your driveway to the visitors by the hour | v: achievement | sphere: faith.B | chance: 65
- R | join the crowd at the window and sing with them until late | v: stimulation | sphere: faith.R | chance: 65
- G | go with your grandparent each evening, and light a candle beside them | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: faith.G | chance: 65
- RG | trust what your heart says about it, and say so to anyone who asks | v: self-direction, tradition | pushes: belief | sphere: faith.RG | chance: 55
- UB | sell your sharpest photographs of the window to the papers | v: achievement, self-direction | sphere: faith.UB | chance: 55
- UG | say nothing against the healing, and simply keep your grandparent company | v: benevolence | pushes: close | sphere: faith.GU | chance: 55
- WB | help the council set up parking and first aid for the crowds | v: security, benevolence | sphere: faith.WB | chance: 55
- WR | warn the crowd not to give up their medicine on the strength of a story | v: benevolence, universalism | lever: voice | sphere: faith.RW | chance: 55
works: Whatever the window shows, the weeks of crowds leave {N} with something {N} values.
works: {Ns} grandparent has good weeks, and {N} is glad to have shared them.
fails: The crowds turn quarrelsome, and the street is sick of the whole business.
fails: The story falls apart in the papers, and those who believed feel foolish.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- rites_cut (pairs D2a)

# world: sphere event rites_cut, selector place, share .3
== ten people at the graveside
tier: life event
sphere: faith
sphere_event: rites_cut
share: .3
holy: mourning
at: faith body
stages: juvenile+
age: 14-100
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
times: World event: rites_cut (sphere faith). Fires for the people of a place when a plague, a famine or a war kills faster than the rites can be held, or gatherings are banned; in such a season perhaps 3 in 10 lose someone close whose rites are cut short (estimate); share .3
likelier: an epidemic with gatherings banned; a war nearby; an old or frail family
rarer: settled years; a young family; a place far from the trouble
gap: 20-80
tone: trouble
life: faith, grief, family
horizon: months
roles: dead, parent
earth: the rules this season allow ten people at a funeral, and you and the rest of the family watch on a screen
scene: The rules this season allow ten people at a funeral. {Ns} family watches {dead}'s on a screen, and no one can hold anyone. The grief has nowhere to go.
scene W: The rites say the whole community must honour the dead. The rules say ten. {N} keeps both as best they can.
scene U: {N} wonders what a rite is for, if it can be cut down to ten people and a camera.
scene B: There are ten places, and the family is arguing over who gets one. {N} could claim a seat.
scene R: {N} cannot bear to watch through glass. Every part of them wants to be in that room.
scene G: {parent} keeps saying the dead will not rest until they are sent off properly.
- W | give up your own place so an older relative can be there | v: benevolence, conformity | sphere: faith.W | chance: 60
- U | write a eulogy, and send it to every relative who cannot come | v: benevolence, self-direction | sphere: faith.U | chance: 60
- B | make sure your side of the family gets the places that count | v: power | mark: made an enemy | sphere: faith.B | chance: 60
- R | stand outside the gate in the rain, as close as the rules allow | v: stimulation, benevolence | sphere: faith.R | chance: 60
- G | promise the family a proper second rite when the rules lift | v: tradition | sphere: faith.G | chance: 60
- BG | pay for a stone and a gathering later that no one will forget | v: tradition, power | lever: fund | sphere: faith.BG | chance: 50
- BR | slip into the back of the hall, and break the rule to be there | v: self-direction, stimulation | mark: broke the law | lever: subvert | sphere: faith.BR | chance: 50
- UR | gather the cousins online that night to tell stories of the dead until late | v: benevolence, stimulation | sphere: faith.UR | chance: 50
- WG | keep the old mourning days at home, with a candle and an empty chair | v: tradition | lever: loyalty | sphere: faith.GW | chance: 50
- WU | ask the faith's leaders for a short rite that families can hold at home | v: conformity, benevolence | lever: voice | pushes: belief | sphere: faith.WU | chance: 50
works: Years later the second rite is held at last, and the family finally says goodbye.
works: The grief finds its way out, slowly, through the small rites the family kept.
fails: The goodbye never quite happens, and {N} carries it unfinished.
fails: The quarrel over the ten places outlasts the mourning.

