earth: a businesswoman leaves her fortune to the faith's food bank, and you are asked to help decide how it is spent
scene: A businesswoman who grew up poor in the town has left her fortune to the faith's food bank. A plaque goes up, and so does a new kitchen, and {N} is asked to sit on the board that decides how the rest is spent.
scene W: The gift comes with a long list of conditions, and {N} means to see every one of them kept.
scene U: {N} wants to know what the town actually needs most before a single thing is bought.
scene B: A fortune with a board around it is a kind of power. {N} sees who wants a seat at that table.
scene R: {N} wants the money working now: hot meals, warm coats, a party for the whole street.
scene G: {N} thinks of the old gifts that still feed the town, made by people long dead, and of what {N} might leave.
